WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.172
Hello and welcome to our video on cross-border logistics for Amazon Selling Partners.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:11.904
This video focuses on logistics when expanding to any store outside of Europe.

00:00:11.904 --> 00:00:19.399
In this video, we will delve into the key topics of international shipping, import and export trade

00:00:19.399 --> 00:00:21.162
and navigating customs regulations.

00:00:21.162 --> 00:00:27.335
We'll also explore how Amazon services, like fulfillment by Amazon, FBA, Amazon Global Logistics,

00:00:27.335 --> 00:00:29.980
AGL, and the partnered carrier program.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.031
PCP can simplify your cross-border operations.

00:00:33.031 --> 00:00:34.329
Let's get started.

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:37.360
What do I need to know before

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:38.810
sending my products?

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:43.160
You must understand the legal requirements and documentation involved

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:49.120
in importing goods into a foreign market or exporting products from your home country.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:53.520
We recommend that you check if you are allowed to sell your products in your destination

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:59.800
store and what additional certificates, testing or documentation you might need beforehand.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:04.680
Import duties and taxes vary from country to country and are typically charged based on

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:06.754
the value of the imported goods.

00:01:06.754 --> 00:01:09.520
When shipping goods, it is important to account

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.165
for import fees, also known as delivery-duty-paid.

00:01:13.165 --> 00:01:16.000
You can ask either your logistic provider

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:21.800
for support or contact an external service provider from our service provider network.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:27.600
Ensuring accurate and complete customs documentation is vital for the efficient clearance of your

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:28.144
shipments.

00:01:28.144 --> 00:01:33.040
Amazon's Seller Central provides guidance on customs documentation, including

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:37.600
commercial invoices, packing lists and certificates of origin.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:42.600
Properly completing these documents facilitates the smooth flow of your shipments through

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.034
customs.

00:01:43.034 --> 00:01:46.509
Customs brokers can support you with customs procedures.

00:01:46.509 --> 00:01:48.680
If you need help finding

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:53.591
a customs broker, you can do so on the service provider network, SPN.

00:01:53.591 --> 00:01:55.480
You can find the SPN

00:01:55.480 --> 00:01:59.455
by going to apps and services and then explore services.

00:01:59.455 --> 00:02:01.840
You have two options for fulfilling

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:02.738
worldwide orders.

00:02:02.738 --> 00:02:07.680
First, fulfilling orders on your own, which means you are responsible

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.840
for sending products to your customers.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.000
And second, fulfilment by Amazon FBA.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.600
FBA is a powerful tool for cross-border logistics.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:20.800
By leveraging FBA, you can store your inventory

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.292
in Amazon's global fulfilment centres.

00:02:23.292 --> 00:02:27.280
Amazon then takes care of order processing, shipping

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:32.640
and customer service, helping you to offer fast and reliable fulfilment to your international

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:33.091
customers.

00:02:33.091 --> 00:02:38.057
This helps you compete with domestic selling partners on delivery speed.

00:02:38.057 --> 00:02:38.960
To ship

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:43.966
your products into our fulfilment network for FBA, you have three options.

00:02:43.966 --> 00:02:44.800
First, using

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:46.268
your own courier.

00:02:46.268 --> 00:02:50.182
Second, using the Amazon Partner Carrier programme, PCP.

00:02:50.182 --> 00:02:51.160
The programme

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:53.768
enables you to send small parcels.

00:02:53.768 --> 00:02:57.680
Please note this is only available for specific countries.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:00.880
You can find more information on our help pages.

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:06.920
Or third, using Amazon Global Logistics, AGL, which supports selling partners with sending

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.440
shipments from CN to the US, UK and Europe.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:13.960
If you wish to find a third-party courier,

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:18.440
check out the service provider network where you will find international shipping companies

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.115
who support your shipping route.

00:03:20.115 --> 00:03:23.800
When creating a shipping plan, you get an address, an Amazon

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:29.000
fulfilment centre in your destination store, to where you send your shipment.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:33.660
In practice, it's no different to sending a shipment to any address worldwide.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:40.400
AGL offers FBA selling partners a comprehensive shipping solution from China to the US, UK

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.480
and Europe via Air and Ocean.

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:45.600
This service ships directly from China into our fulfilment

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.560
centres or your own warehouses.

00:03:47.560 --> 00:03:51.480
Selling partners can select this service when creating a shipment

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:54.024
on Seller Central or Shipper Central.

00:03:54.024 --> 00:03:57.840
The AGL service includes shipment pick up in origin,

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:03.720
palletization, if required, export import customs clearance and domestic delivery in

00:04:03.720 --> 00:04:08.240
the destination country to either FBA or your warehouse.

00:04:08.240 --> 00:04:13.600
We also offer the Amazon partnered carrier programme PCP for selling partners who, for

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.605
example, wish to ship directly from the UK or Germany to the US.

00:04:18.605 --> 00:04:19.760
This programme offers

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:25.160
an integrated small parcel shipping service through Seller Central with automated booking,

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.443
tracking and payment.

00:04:26.443 --> 00:04:30.720
Using this programme, you can replenish inventory on Seller Central

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:33.696
without needing to sort out shipping options offline.

00:04:33.696 --> 00:04:35.680
Please check our help pages for

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:36.427
other locales.

00:04:36.427 --> 00:04:41.280
You can create your shipment into FBA on Seller Central using our shipment

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.228
creation workflow.

00:04:42.228 --> 00:04:47.440
To get started, go to your Seller Central, navigate to inventory,

00:04:47.440 --> 00:04:51.394
FBA inventory, shipments and then send to Amazon.

00:04:51.394 --> 00:04:54.360
First, provide your ship from address

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.680
and indicate whether you will be shipping individual or case-packed items.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:04:59.400
Then enter

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:04.320
the quantities for each item and decide whether you will prep the units or you would like

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.909
Amazon to prep them for you, for a per unit fee.

00:05:07.909 --> 00:05:10.520
We have a more extensive guide on packaging,

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:14.120
prep and labelling requirements in Seller University for the US.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:16.280
How to ship your products from

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:17.307
EU to US.

00:05:17.307 --> 00:05:22.440
If you handle returns on your own, you either need a prepaid shipping label or

00:05:22.440 --> 00:05:25.491
a domestic return address in your destination store.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:28.160
If you use fulfilment by Amazon, Amazon

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:31.253
takes care of your returns and inventory removal.

00:05:31.253 --> 00:05:33.960
Amazon offers resources and tools, such as

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:39.120
the returns and refunds policies and the Seller Central help and customer service, to help

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:43.120
you handle returns and provide excellent customer support across borders.

00:05:43.120 --> 00:05:45.120
You now have a deeper

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:49.350
understanding of cross-border logistics for Amazon selling partners.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:50.760
Remember to explore

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:57.960
the resources available on Seller Central and leverage services like FBA, AgL or PCP to

00:05:57.960 --> 00:05:59.550
streamline your operations.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:04.320
By effectively managing your logistics and complying with customs

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:09.139
regulations, you can expand your business globally and reach customers around the world.

00:06:09.139 --> 00:06:09.880
If you

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:14.800
have any further questions or need additional assistance, make sure to utilise the resources

00:06:14.800 --> 00:06:20.440
provided by Seller Central, the Seller University and Global Selling pages that you can find

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.010
under the link, sell.

00:06:22.010 --> 00:06:22.402
amazon.

00:06:22.402 --> 00:06:22.795
co.

00:06:22.795 --> 00:06:23.188
uk.

00:06:23.188 --> 00:06:28.090
Thanks for watching and happy selling in the Amazon store.
